Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 05:32:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(android): resolve CapacitorApp ReferenceError on native
 builds

The 'import { App as CapacitorApp }' was causing a ReferenceError on Android builds because bundlers and Capacitor APIs don't always align well with aliased module scopes within conditional blocks.
To fix this:
1. Replaced the aliased import with the standard 'import { App }'.
2. Abstracted native app lifecycle listener logic into 'lib/native/appLifecycle.ts' so the React components do not attempt to hold or parse native plugin references, which also fixes improper callback cleanup causing potential memory leaks.
3. Updated 'DiaryLayout.tsx' to use the asynchronous register logic and correctly cleanup those event listeners.
4. Wrapped 'NativeBiometric' calls in a try-catch to avoid uncaught exceptions failing to initialize biometric unlock.
5. Added an ErrorBoundary globally using React Router's 'errorElement' property so that uncaught exceptions present a friendly error UI instead of failing to render.
6. Updated 'package.json' to ensure 'tsc --noEmit' executes prior to native Android builds for CI protection.
